Keep a shared first as 0.
Keep a shared second as 0.
Keep a shared rank as 0.
Keep a shared leftvalue as 0.
Keep a shared rightvalue as 0.
Keep a shared divisor as 0.
Keep a shared multiple as 0.
Keep a shared counted as 0.
Keep a shared answer as 0.
Set first to 2.
Set second to 3.
Set rank to 4.
To reduce.
If rightvalue is 0, set divisor to leftvalue, return.
The remainder is leftvalue modulo rightvalue.
Set leftvalue to rightvalue.
Set rightvalue to remainder.
Reduce.

To tally with spot (a whole number).
Set counted to spot divided by first plus spot divided by second minus spot divided by multiple.

To seek from low (a whole number) with high (a whole number).
If low is at least high, set answer to low, return.
The middle is (low plus high) divided by 2.
Tally with middle.
If counted is at least rank, seek from low with middle, return.
If counted is less than rank, seek from middle plus 1 with high.

Set leftvalue to first.
Set rightvalue to second.
Reduce.
Set multiple to first divided by divisor times second.
Seek from 1 with first times rank.
Show answer.
